 "task": "stack the yellow cube first, then the red cube on top, then the blue cube on top",
 "success": "cubes stacked bottom to top in the order ['yellow', 'red', 'blue'], each within 1.5 cm of the one below and 5 cm above it, upright; gripper clear and stable fresh poses for 3 wall-clock seconds (3 mm / 5 degree drift limit)",
 "api": "def run(robot, task): ...     # task.text is the task in words; import nothing but math\nrobot.arm.joints() -> list[float] (radians); robot.arm.pose() -> Pose(position xyz m, orientation xyzw)\nrobot.arm.move_pose(xyz, orientation=None)   # orientation: roll, pitch, yaw or xyzw; None keeps the current one\nrobot.arm.move_linear(dx=0, dy=0, dz=0)      # straight line, metres\nrobot.arm.move_joints(positions); robot.arm.home()\nrobot.gripper.open(); robot.gripper.close(); robot.gripper.set(value); robot.gripper.range() -> (closed, open)\nrobot.scene.objects([\"cube\", \"bowl\"]) -> [SceneObject(id, name, position, size, yaw)]   # world metres, box centre\nrobot.observe() -> keyframe path; robot.log(text)\nMotion calls block and raise RobotCallError (status PLANNING_FAILED, EXECUTION_FAILED or TIMEOUT).\nEvery call goes to the trial's trace.jsonl, with a keyframe before and after each motion call.\n",
 "budget": {
  "iterations": 2,
  "candidates_per_round": 2,
  "dev_trials": 3,
  "heldout_trials": 5,
  "threshold": 0.8,
  "candidates_submitted": 0,
  "candidates_left": 4
 },
 "status": "idle",
 "frozen": null,
 "library": [
  "# Measured facts about this arm and bench (from earlier sessions on the same lab)\n\n- `arm.pose()` and `move_pose()` address `gripper_base`, the jaw's mount. The finger pads are 0.078 m\n  further along the approach (the tool's local +z). A top-down grasp at a cube's centre height needs the\n  mount at `z_cube + 0.078`; a release 1 cm above a seat needs `z_seat + 0.078 + 0.01`.\n- Gravity sag: the arm settles 2\u20134 cm below and up to 3 cm beside a commanded pose. Measure the error\n  with `arm.pose()` after a planned move and re-issue `move_pose` with the error added (0.7 gain,\n  2\u20133 re-aims converge to ~1 cm). `move_linear` plans from the measured pose and cannot cancel the sag;\n  a straight move ends about one sag lower than commanded.\n- The gripper is non-blocking: `gripper.open()`/`close()` return in ~10 ms. Wait (about 20\u201330\n  `arm.pose()` reads, or ~2 s) before lifting or retreating, or the jaw lifts the cube it just released.\n- Object positions read while a cube is in the jaw are biased by ~1 cm (occlusion): do not correct a\n  placement from them; use the tool error measured at closing instead.\n- Obstacle map: every object is an obstacle until `scene.clear(id)`; clear each cube you will touch or\n  put something on, and the one you are carrying is an obstacle again outside its cleared zone, so\n  re-clear the held cube over its destination (or the carry is refused with PLANNING_FAILED). Cleared\n  objects are invisible to the planner: a planned move can sweep the jaw through a finished tower, so\n  travel in straight lines (`move_linear`) at a clear height (tower top + 16 cm) over built levels.\n- Reach: a rise to 0.25\u20130.30 m over objects far from the base (x > 0.28 m) often has no IK solution.\n  A build spot at about 0.20 m in x (10 cm from every object) keeps every level reachable; when a rise\n  is refused, slide to 9 cm before the target, rise there, then finish the slide.\n- Cubes are 5 cm; stacked levels sit 5 cm apart. The judge wants each cube within 1.5 cm of the one below,\n  upright, and then the gripper more than 16 cm from every cube and the tower still for 3 s: end the\n  program with a verified 2 cm rise after the release and a 20 cm retreat toward the base.\n- A passing program took 90\u2013100 s per trial; the program timeout is 300 s.\n"
 ]
}
